Alright I finally ascended.  Not save/restore stuff, no polypiling, 
no bones file trickery, didn't even use any self-polymorphing or my ring
of conflict.  I used the bell of opening abuse a little, but not much 
because I thought my hit points were already high enough (after the Priest
quest).  This is really only the third time I even came close:

 No  Points     Name                                                   Hp [max]
  1    5203916  Peter-P ascended to demigod-hood.                     467 [502]
  2    1096089  Peter-P died in Gehennom on level 31 [max 34].        501 [501]
                Killed by a touch of death.
  3     465090  Peter-P died in The Quest on level 20 [max 16].         - [575]
                Killed by Nalzok.

Highlights, possible spoilers, and long boring musings follow:

























I got lucky this game and found a magic lamp early.  I blessed it, and
used my wish for a blessed figurine of Archon.  He gave me a sheild of
reflection, and a Sunsword.  At this point, a brilliant (?) plan occured
to me:

   I was currently only at Exp level 3.  How about I try to sneak down
   through the mines without killing anything (let the Archon kill
   everything for me).  Arrive at the shop level, and let my pet kill
   all the shopkeepers.  Use all their money to donate to the temple
   Priest to get amazing AC (because 400*level 3 isn't that really all
   that much).

Well, here's what actually happened:

   I accidentally killed a few things (in fact the turn right after I
   decided not to kill anything, I hit a newt, killed it, and went to
   Exp level 4).  By the time a got the shop level, I was at Exp level 5.
   My Archon killed one shop keeper, and I took the money.  I went to
   the priest, and carefully locked the door behind me so the Archon 
   couldn't follow me in.  I donated $2000 a few times, and then went
   back to let the Archon kill the other shopkeepers.  Unfortunately,
   when I was leaving the temple, I wasn't being too careful, and my
   Archon went in and killed the Priest.  Oh well.

So I got reasonable intrinsic armor class out of that, plus lots of
stuff from the shops.  Since I was at level 5 and lawful I then took
a long sword (which my Archon got from a guard), and dipped it in the
fountain to get Excalibur.  I found a magic marker in the shops, so I
blessed it, and used it to write enchant weapon scrolls to get my 
Excalibur up to +7.  I also found a magic harp and a magic flute
which both came in handy later...

Later on, I was heading down through the dungeons of doom, I ate 
something I shouldn't have, and got intrinsic teleport.  I had found 
another magic marker, so I cursed the second one, and used it to write
cursed genocide scrolls.  I used them to summon tengu's, which my
Archon killed and I ate.  I think I got teleport control after the
second scroll.

When I found the Quest Portal, I was only at Exp level 13.  I kept
going down until I found an alter.  I used a few wands of create 
monster (plus a few spellbooks) to summon monsters, get experience
points, and get some goodies from my God.  By the time I got to 
Exp level 14, I had pretty much all the lawful artifacts.

I then made a good decision: I decided that I wasn't ready for Nalzok
(the Priest quest bad-guy) yet.  I'd gotten killed by Nalzok in my
previous game, so I not to try him until I'd gotten an Amulet of 
Lifesaving and some better armor.  I decided to do the castle first.
But I did the first few quest levels first, to get all those Wraiths.

After getting to Exp level 30, I went back to the Dungeons of Doom and
headed for the castle.  My Archon got killed a little later.  I have no
idea what did it - I couldn't find anything nasty on the level.

So I kept going down, and had my closest call of the game on the 
Medusa level.  I had no levitation ring, so I froze the lake to 
get to her.  I put on my blindfold, and killed her (I think she
stoned herself with my sheild).  There were a few nasty monsters
hanging around (a dragon and a few other guys).  My hit points were
getting pretty low, so I decided to run away and recover.  Just as
I was leaving, I got swallowed by (I think) a purple worm.  

After he'd digested me a few times I was down to 35 hit points. He
seemed to do about 40 points of damage per round, so I was noticably
nervous.  Hitting him wasn't working, so I decided to be more 
creative (a departure from my normal hack and slash approach).  

I started up a new game in Wizard mode, to see what would get me out
in one turn (guaranteed).  The first thing I found was that a wand
of digging got you out.  I decided not to try that because:
  a) my wand of digging was in my sack and I didn't think I'd
     have time to get it out.
  b) the worm often swallows you again the very next turn.
Instead I found that using a magic harp would tame him, and cause
him to spit me out.  So I tried it in my real game.

MISTAKE! It didn't work.  I'm not sure why (maybe the taming only
works sometimes), but in this game the worm kept digesting me.  I
was down to 5 HP!  So now I definitely didn't have time to get
anything out of my sack.  Fortunately, I did have a magic flute
handy.  I used that and it put him to sleep.  He stopped digesting
me, and I killed him with a few more whacks from Excalibur.  When I
got out, all the other nasties were also asleep, so I managed to
recover.

When I got to the castle, I used my magic harp to tame a bunch of
monsters by the gate, so I had about a dozen pets helping me with
that level.  I got the wand of wishing, wished for an amulet of 
life saving, +3 GDSM, fireproof speed boots, and a ring of 
levitation.  I then went back to do the quest with a Wand of 
Wishing (1). 

To make a long story short (too late), I went back and did the 
quest but Nalzok did cost me an Amulet of life saving.  What 
happened was I fell through to his level from the one above, and
he started attacking me before I even knew where the up stair 
were.  He made 3 clones of himself, but eventually I killed them 
all (I think I used my magic harp to tame many of his pets).  I 
then used my WoW to get another Amulet of Life saving (never 
needed it though).

I was then reading through this group and found that I should
have been using Grayswandir against him, not Excalibur.  Live
and learn.  I enchanted my Grayswandir up to +7, and used it
against all the other major demons in the game.


Despite what I've heard in this group, it is possible to win
3.1 without level teleporting.  Unlike older nethacks, there
were downstairs on all the level up to 51.  I was assuming that
eventually I'd run out of downstairs and have to level teleport
to level 55 where the "vibrating space" was.  Well, in this
game I just stumbled across the vibrating space on level 51.

I then went back up, finally found Vlad's tower on level 40 (?),
and got the candelabrum.  I went to the fake wizard level where 
there was a protal to the Wiz's tower.  I then killed him, got
the book, and went down to 51.  Once I'd opened the stairs down,
I had some trouble finding the door to the inner sanctuary, but
aside from that had little trouble.  I think that was mainly 
because of +7 Grayswandir, plus pretty good AC.

The wizard stole the Amulet once on the way up, but I killed 
him a few levels later, and got it back.  The water level was 
the most interesting of the endgame (The confused/gold 
detection to locate the Portal didn't work as expected, 
because the Portal moves).  I was a little worried about the 
water level because I didn't have an Amulet of magical 
breathing.  I took off the Amulet of Yendor, and put on my 
Amulet of life saving just in case.  While I sat in the bubble 
I tried zapping my WofW(0) to get a wish for an Amulet of 
magical breathing.  Before I got one, the bubble just floated
me over to the Portal.

In the final level I found the lawful altar on the third try.
All in all, nethack 3.1 is a really good game.  It takes a 
very long time to win (I think this game was about 3 weeks
of playing off and on).  I think the game balance is just 
fine, even later on in the game, because after all, I
wouldn't have wanted to lose after 3 weeks of playing (unless
I made a big mistake and deserved to lose).

I finished with lots of goodies, almost all the intrinsics, 
and a scroll of genocide I couldn't decide what to do with
(I'd already done L, n, g, and c).
 
Now I can forget about this game for a while.




Or maybe I should try to win as a Tourist ;-)
